fP  
.SH "Heads up!"
.PP
\fBOrder of arguments\fP

.PP
When the \fRmin\fP is larger than the \fRmax\fP, values will be flipped to create a valid range:

.PP
.PP
.nf
toRegexRange('51', '29');
.fi
.PP

.PP
Is effectively flipped to:

.PP
.PP
.nf
toRegexRange('29', '51');
//=> 29|[3\-4][0\-9]|5[0\-1]
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBSteps / increments\fP

.PP
This library does not support steps (increments)\&. A pr to add support would be welcome\&.
.SH "History"
.PP
.SS "v2\&.0\&.0 - 2017-04-21"
\fBNew features\fP

.PP
Adds support for zero-padding!
.SS "v1\&.0\&.0"
\fBOptimizations\fP

.PP
Repeating ranges are now grouped using quantifiers\&. rocessing time is roughly the same, but the generated regex is much smaller, which should result in faster matching\&.
